# Testing

Vitest (`npm test`), tests in `tests/*.test.ts`. CI order: `type-check` → `check:i18n` → `check:docs` → `check:env` → `test` → `build-only`.

- **Behavior changes must extend the matching test file.** Covered contracts: API client + CSRF + 419/settle retry (`client.test.ts`), retry policy (`netRetry.test.ts`), nonce single-flight and cookie-settle gate (`csrf.test.ts`), shell hydration (`shellHydrate.test.ts`), menu-edit hydrate (`navigationHydrate.test.ts`), cross-tab logout (`authCrossTabLogout.test.ts`), Echo authorizer + channel registry (`echo.test.ts`, `echoHelpers.test.ts`, `channelRegistry.test.ts`, `echoConventions.test.ts`), headers/URL (`requestHeaders.test.ts`, `baseUrl.test.ts`), i18n plumbing (`i18n.test.ts`, `settingsI18n.test.ts`, `translatableLocaleMap.test.ts`), safe URLs/redirects, vTual claims hub + JSON-LD + presentation, breadcrumbs.
- Add a test file per **contract surface** (`tests/<area>.test.ts`), not per component.
- Tests stub `fetch` — no live API, deterministic and offline.
- Component rendering tests are not the norm. **Exception: DOM contracts** opt into jsdom per file (`// @vitest-environment jsdom`, e.g. `headMetaJsonLd.test.ts`); the suite default stays `node`. A pure decision belongs in `src/utils/*` where node can test it.
- Verifying vendor-widget CSS means measuring against a **vendor-built** DOM (real jQuery + select2 in headless Chrome). A hand-written harness measures a DOM the library never creates.

Details: [docs/testing.md](../../docs/testing.md).
